' #FISSURE-PLUGIN 1
' #NAME "Generic Language Adapter"
' #TYPE LANGUAGE
' #REQUIRES FILE.READ
' #REQUIRES GRAPH.WRITE
'
' RFC section 7.4: "A built-in reference ArcoBASIC adapter must provide Tier 0 support for
' languages and DSLs with no dedicated adapter... Fissure must degrade to conservative generic
' analysis, not declare a language unsupported." Tier 0's own ceiling (section 7.3): "Files,
' configured probe associations, build links, runtime observations" -- this adapter registers
' exactly one thing, a File node per tracked file, and nothing about their relationships to each
' other (no import scanning -- that is Tier 1, a dedicated language adapter's job, not this one's).
' Every probe's own declared dependencies (fissure.ab's FISSURE.Probe.DependsOn calls) point at
' the same file ids this adapter creates, which is what lets a plain path-based association work
' at all without any language-specific parsing.

FUNCTION DiscoverFiles()
    paths = FISSURE.Filesystem.Walk()
    FOR path IN paths
        ignored = FISSURE.Graph.Node(path, "file")
    NEXT
END FUNCTION
